<title>JAPAN: Sakura Bank forgives loans to two mortgage firms.</title>
<headline>Sakura Bank forgives loans to two mortgage firms.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sakura Bank Ltd said on Monday that it had forgiven loans of 280.23 billion yen which it had extended to two housing loan companies.  </p>
<p>The loans forgiven were those extended to Nippon Housing Loan Co Ltd and Housing Loan Service Co Ltd, Sakura said in a statement.</p>
<p>Sakura said forgiving the loans would not affect its earnings in the year to March 31, 1997.</p>
</text>
